comment_data.body:
@lupont, @xigoi, sorry for the long delay. Didn't want to implement such big functionality without tests to check if nothing got broken. And in turn writing tests was a daunting task, so it took a while. But almost all modules are now covered with tests, including 'mini.surround'. So I decided to implement it right away.

The approach I decided to use is through [config.custom_surroundings](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/297993c40e93bd155d72424e3a1abeefb3be344e/doc/mini.txt#L3784) option. Both of your Latex related requests should be possible with the following setup:
```lua
require('mini.surround').setup({
  custom_surroundings = {
    S = {
      input = { [[\begin{(%w*)}.-\end{%1}]], [[^\begin{.-}().-()\end{.-}$]] },
      output = function()
        local latex_name = MiniSurround.user_input('Latex object name')
        return { left = ([[\begin{%s}]]):format(latex_name), right = ([[\end{%s}]]):format(latex_name) }
      end,
    },
    L = {
      input = { [[\%w+%b{}]], '^.-{().*()}$' },
      output = function()
        local cmd_name = MiniSurround.user_input('Latex command name')
        if cmd_name == nil then return nil end
        return { left = ([[\%s{]]):format(cmd_name), right = '}' }
      end,
    },
  },
})
```

Yes, a little bit complex, but that's the price for customization involving querying user for command name.

**Edit**: The setup was adjusted for `input` values to follow the since changed surrounding specification. The `\begin{}...\end{}` surrounding is also changed from `l` to `S` identifier because it conflicts with default ["find previous"](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4035ef97407a6661ae9ff913ff980e271a658502/doc/mini-surround.txt#L512) suffixed variants (like `sdl`, `srl`, etc.). To use `l` as identifier make sure that `config.mappings.suffix_last` is not `'l'`.
